1
00:00:03,310 --> 00:00:08,270
(Even the Student Council Has Its Holes!)

2
00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:37,880
All right.

3
00:01:38,610 --> 00:01:39,650
(Student Council Room)

4
00:01:39,650 --> 00:01:40,610
The Next Day.

5
00:01:40,610 --> 00:01:40,870
(Student Council Room)

6
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:43,450
All right, that's a breather!

7
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:46,080
Michinoku, what do you want for lunch?

8
00:01:46,980 --> 00:01:48,810
Oh, right.

9
00:01:49,580 --> 00:01:49,830
(Tosei Academy Student Council)
(Lemon) (Thinking back, we've come a long way)

10
00:01:50,590 --> 00:01:50,840
(Tosei Academy Student Council)

11
00:01:51,590 --> 00:01:51,840
(Tosei Academy Student Council) (Its legs
grow out of the middle of its body)

12
00:01:55,050 --> 00:01:55,950
Onigiri.

13
00:01:56,310 --> 00:01:56,740
Huh?

14
00:01:57,480 --> 00:01:58,260
Have some.

15
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:02,760
(Episode 7: Komaro's Challenge)

16
00:02:03,210 --> 00:02:06,170
Is this a prototype for the ones
we're gonna sell at school?

17
00:02:06,170 --> 00:02:06,830
Yeah.

18
00:02:06,830 --> 00:02:07,860
Give it a taste.

19
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:08,880
(Suggestion Box)

20
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:10,620
We got a suggestion from Suggestion Box,

21
00:02:10,889 --> 00:02:12,960
asking for some cheaper options.

22
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:14,550
I see.

23
00:02:14,890 --> 00:02:15,910
Seriously,

24
00:02:16,230 --> 00:02:19,280
our School Store and Cafeteria
are going to hike up the prices.

25
00:02:19,550 --> 00:02:21,100
The baseball club mentioned it, too.

26
00:02:21,320 --> 00:02:22,580
That's true.

27
00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:23,960
But, for a moment,

28
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:26,780
I thought it was a 'Homemade Lunch
Like a Loving Wife' for you, Ume.

29
00:02:27,110 --> 00:02:28,170
Huh!? No, no, no...!

30
00:02:29,220 --> 00:02:30,390
I did think so.

31
00:02:30,850 --> 00:02:31,950
But, Komaro,

32
00:02:32,350 --> 00:02:34,620
how exactly are you planning to sell these?

33
00:02:34,930 --> 00:02:35,530
Oh.

34
00:02:35,670 --> 00:02:36,000
(Onigiri)

35
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,060
(Onigiri)
I'll make them in the morning myself,

36
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:41,100
and set up a shop on the ground
during the lunch break.

37
00:02:41,230 --> 00:02:42,020
Yourself?!

38
00:02:42,020 --> 00:02:43,150
That's a bit much...

39
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:46,980
Well, we could always ask
a local vendor to make them.

40
00:02:46,980 --> 00:02:50,990
Each one costs about 40 yen to make...

41
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:52,060
So I'm selling each one for 40 yen?

42
00:02:52,060 --> 00:02:52,810
(Huh...)
So I'm selling each one for 40 yen?

43
00:02:52,810 --> 00:02:52,860
So I'm selling each one for 40 yen?

44
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:53,380
(Ingredient Cost: 40 yen,
Selling Price: 40 yen,)

45
00:02:53,380 --> 00:02:55,320
(Profit: 0 yen)
That's a 100% cost ratio!

46
00:02:55,790 --> 00:02:58,530
For now, let's not worry about the details.

47
00:02:58,780 --> 00:02:59,750
Let's eat.

48
00:03:00,070 --> 00:03:00,810
Sounds good!

49
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:04,570
Let's see if this can satisfy my refined palate!

50
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:05,620
There he goes again!

51
00:03:06,170 --> 00:03:09,170
You talk a big game,
but you've got the palate of a kid.

52
00:03:09,430 --> 00:03:11,020
What are you talking about?

53
00:03:11,020 --> 00:03:12,130
I'm very picky about what I eat!

54
00:03:12,130 --> 00:03:12,960
(Bleh)
I'm very picky about what I eat!

55
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:13,020
I'm very picky about what I eat!

56
00:03:13,230 --> 00:03:15,210
Oh, by the way, do you have any mayo?

57
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:17,730
Fried chicken is pretty pricey, y'know

58
00:03:17,730 --> 00:03:18,620
Sorry.

59
00:03:18,890 --> 00:03:19,810
Such a kid’s palate.

60
00:03:20,170 --> 00:03:20,600
(Today's Pattern)

61
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:21,830
Let's taste it.

62
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:24,250
This is delicious!

63
00:03:24,410 --> 00:03:25,580
It really is!

64
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:26,850
The seasoning's just right.

65
00:03:27,090 --> 00:03:27,880
But...

66
00:03:28,670 --> 00:03:29,810
What's... this?

67
00:03:30,870 --> 00:03:33,520
That's dried squid. I steamed it.

68
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:34,510
Dried squid?

69
00:03:34,690 --> 00:03:36,020
I used some

70
00:03:36,020 --> 00:03:38,530
that was lying around at
the teacher's house to keep costs down.

71
00:03:38,530 --> 00:03:40,240
Oh, so we still had some left.

72
00:03:40,540 --> 00:03:42,410
Wait, is this even safe to eat...?

73
00:03:43,170 --> 00:03:44,720
Thanks for the meal!

74
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,200
- Yeah, it was good,
- To whet everyone's appetite,

75
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:47,830
- But,
- To whet everyone's appetite,

76
00:03:47,830 --> 00:03:50,060
- I'm not sure this is really sellable...
- you need more fried chicken.

77
00:03:50,060 --> 00:03:51,110
- Yeah, I agree.
- I write it down.

78
00:03:51,420 --> 00:03:53,100
Even if we outsource the cooking,

79
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:55,100
we'll still need to figure out the price and fillings.

80
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:56,800
Dried squid is probably a bit much...

81
00:03:58,200 --> 00:04:01,050
So we need to come up with
an affordable filling that'll be a hit.

82
00:04:01,050 --> 00:04:02,530
How are we supposed to do that?

83
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:02,910
(Slide!)

84
00:04:02,910 --> 00:04:04,110
Hey, everyone!

85
00:04:04,340 --> 00:04:05,660
What's up?

86
00:04:05,660 --> 00:04:07,130
What's with all the long faces?

87
00:04:07,410 --> 00:04:09,390
Well, long story short.

88
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:10,140
Hmm, I see.

89
00:04:10,260 --> 00:04:12,820
That has been an issue for a while.

90
00:04:12,890 --> 00:04:13,250
(Hmm)

91
00:04:13,250 --> 00:04:15,770
That's all the more reason
I want to make this happen.

92
00:04:16,670 --> 00:04:18,029
Why don't you come over to my place?

93
00:04:18,940 --> 00:04:20,019
Why?

94
00:04:20,529 --> 00:04:21,610
Oh, that reminds me...

95
00:04:22,430 --> 00:04:23,190
Sorry,

96
00:04:23,190 --> 00:04:24,680
I guess I never told you!

97
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:28,060
You know Kotobuki,
that restaurant near the station?

98
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:29,230
(Kotobuki Restaurant)
That's my family's place.

99
00:04:29,350 --> 00:04:30,130
Eh?

100
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:32,960
We've got all the ingredients
and equipment there,

101
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:35,550
so it'd be a good place to experiment
and do some research, wouldn't it?

102
00:04:35,780 --> 00:04:36,550
That's amazing!

103
00:04:36,550 --> 00:04:37,500
Sounds great.

104
00:04:37,770 --> 00:04:39,670
That's great, Komaro.

105
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:40,900
Thank you!

106
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:42,410
Do we get free staff meals?

107
00:04:42,740 --> 00:04:44,290
Well, we'll take you up on that!

108
00:04:44,460 --> 00:04:46,460
We'll all come by sometime soon.

109
00:04:46,610 --> 00:04:46,980
Okay,

110
00:04:47,300 --> 00:04:47,760
got it.

111
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:48,180
(Chatting)

112
00:04:48,180 --> 00:04:50,150
- Kotobuki... Oh, I get it now.
- I've been there a few times.

113
00:04:50,150 --> 00:04:52,210
- I see.
- It'll be my first time. - Do we get staff meals? Huh?

114
00:04:52,270 --> 00:04:52,520
(Rumble...)

115
00:04:52,520 --> 00:04:53,220
(Rumble...)
Wait, does this mean

116
00:04:53,220 --> 00:04:53,430
(Rumble...)

117
00:04:53,430 --> 00:04:56,040
Mizunoe is coming over to my place, too?

118
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:57,670
What am I gonna do?

119
00:04:57,870 --> 00:04:59,450
(Rumble...)
Big Sis, you're so loud!

120
00:04:59,480 --> 00:04:59,980
(I also tried salt candies and stuff)

121
00:04:59,980 --> 00:05:02,690
I also tried salt candies and stuff.

122
00:05:02,690 --> 00:05:03,950
Ugh.

123
00:05:03,950 --> 00:05:06,100
They're good for preventing heatstroke.

124
00:05:06,340 --> 00:05:07,690
Well, it's winter, though...

125
00:05:08,550 --> 00:05:09,620
(Kotobuki Restaurant)
And Then,

126
00:05:09,620 --> 00:05:11,630
On the Day of the Onigiri Trial Run.

127
00:05:11,700 --> 00:05:11,980
(Rustle, Clunk)

128
00:05:11,980 --> 00:05:12,620
(Rustle, Clunk)
All right!

129
00:05:12,620 --> 00:05:14,510
That should be all the ingredients.

130
00:05:14,690 --> 00:05:17,910
Next, we need to get a worktable
and a knife ready for Komaro—

131
00:05:17,910 --> 00:05:18,790
(Rustle, Clunk)

132
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:22,450
(President's Mother (38), Mayuki Kotobuki)
What have you been up to this whole time, Mom?

133
00:05:22,840 --> 00:05:23,250
(Thud! Clunk! Rattle)

134
00:05:23,250 --> 00:05:26,660
(Thud! Clunk! Rattle)
Well, your friends are coming over, right?

135
00:05:26,660 --> 00:05:29,480
I thought I'd bring out some
of my special treats for the occasion...

136
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:31,800
No, we don't have time for that! Save it for later!

137
00:05:32,020 --> 00:05:33,340
We should focus on getting ready...

138
00:05:34,270 --> 00:05:37,040
The yokan from Unrindo and the yokan from Kuraya...

139
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:38,270
They're all mixed together!

140
00:05:38,270 --> 00:05:39,900
I need to sort them out!

141
00:05:39,900 --> 00:05:41,090
Can it wait?!

142
00:05:42,040 --> 00:05:43,660
Sorry, Hisako.

143
00:05:43,660 --> 00:05:46,830
I'm getting worked up over the wrong things again.

144
00:05:47,160 --> 00:05:48,790
Come on! Pull yourself together.

145
00:05:48,790 --> 00:05:50,450
Today's important!

146
00:05:50,450 --> 00:05:51,620
Right!

147
00:05:51,620 --> 00:05:57,330
The customers have finally started
complimenting me lately.

148
00:05:57,330 --> 00:05:57,620
(Yes)

149
00:05:57,620 --> 00:05:58,700
(Yes)
Complimenting you?

150
00:05:58,700 --> 00:05:59,580
(Busy, Well-endowed)
That's right!

151
00:05:59,580 --> 00:06:01,700
They say,
'Mayuki, you're quite something.'

152
00:06:01,700 --> 00:06:02,620
(Busy, Well-endowed)
Amazing! [Well-endowed]

153
00:06:02,620 --> 00:06:04,080
That's definitely not what they meant.

154
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:06,620
You said you'd help, so take this seriously!

155
00:06:06,620 --> 00:06:09,160
I want to help my underclassman.

156
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:10,200
Go wash the rice.

157
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:11,500
Okay!

158
00:06:11,750 --> 00:06:15,000
Komaro's usually so shy,
but she really wants to give this her best.

159
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:19,910
You really take after your father
in that way, Hisako.

160
00:06:19,910 --> 00:06:21,500
So cool.

161
00:06:21,500 --> 00:06:24,200
He's always been like that.

162
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:26,200
- He really is so cool. So, so cool.

163
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:28,410
- I told you to keep your hands moving!
- He really is so cool. So, so cool.

164
00:06:28,620 --> 00:06:30,750
But there's another reason

165
00:06:30,750 --> 00:06:33,410
you're getting so worked up, isn't there?

166
00:06:33,660 --> 00:06:35,330
Ume Mizunoe.

167
00:06:35,330 --> 00:06:36,660
How did you know?

168
00:06:36,660 --> 00:06:38,620
Taiga told me.

169
00:06:38,620 --> 00:06:39,950
Taiga!

170
00:06:39,950 --> 00:06:43,000
Lately, my sister has been talking about
this guy called Ume nonstop!

171
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:43,910
And that's not all...

172
00:06:43,910 --> 00:06:45,660
It seems like

173
00:06:45,660 --> 00:06:47,330
you two are pretty lovey-dovey.

174
00:06:47,330 --> 00:06:50,870
Uh... No.

175
00:06:50,870 --> 00:06:52,000
Huh?

176
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,200
Because I thought I heard something

177
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:54,260
about you being taken in...

178
00:06:54,260 --> 00:06:55,500
(Busted)
about you being taken in...

179
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:55,770
(Busted)

180
00:06:55,910 --> 00:06:57,200
I knew it!

181
00:06:57,200 --> 00:06:58,120
So that means...

182
00:06:58,120 --> 00:07:00,330
- You two are together, right?
- No, we're not!

183
00:07:01,370 --> 00:07:03,040
You two... did it?

184
00:07:03,040 --> 00:07:04,620
Let me explain!

185
00:07:04,910 --> 00:07:06,410
And that's the whole story.

186
00:07:06,620 --> 00:07:07,580
Oh.

187
00:07:07,580 --> 00:07:10,660
So the whole 'being taken in' thing was just a joke.

188
00:07:10,660 --> 00:07:12,080
Why are you so disappointed?

189
00:07:12,080 --> 00:07:15,790
I got married when I was about your age, Hisako.

190
00:07:15,790 --> 00:07:20,080
So I've always hoped you'd find
someone special someday, too.

191
00:07:20,080 --> 00:07:21,750
I just got so excited...

192
00:07:21,750 --> 00:07:23,160
Sorry about that.

193
00:07:23,160 --> 00:07:28,200
W-well, if you mean it that way, maybe a little?

194
00:07:28,620 --> 00:07:29,950
That's wonderful!

195
00:07:29,950 --> 00:07:32,620
I've been getting things ready,

196
00:07:32,620 --> 00:07:34,700
hoping I could get to know Ume better!

197
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:35,540
Look!

198
00:07:35,540 --> 00:07:37,330
The Best of Hisako Photo Album!

199
00:07:37,330 --> 00:07:38,330
Stop it!

200
00:07:38,330 --> 00:07:41,620
(Tug)
I stayed up all night picking these out!

201
00:07:41,620 --> 00:07:43,700
Your idea of cute is seriously messed up, Mom!

202
00:07:43,700 --> 00:07:43,980
Oh, right!

203
00:07:43,980 --> 00:07:44,450
(Sparkle)
Oh, right!

204
00:07:44,450 --> 00:07:46,620
(Sparkle)
There's one more thing!

205
00:07:46,620 --> 00:07:47,190
(Sparkle)

206
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:48,570
You don't have to go that far.

207
00:07:48,570 --> 00:07:49,150
(Thud)
You don't have to go that far.

208
00:07:49,150 --> 00:07:50,250
You don't have to go that far.

209
00:07:50,250 --> 00:07:52,950
I'm the only one who has feelings for him, anyway.

210
00:07:56,370 --> 00:07:57,830
I figured if I wanted to blend in
with the high schoolers,

211
00:07:57,830 --> 00:08:00,370
a school uniform would be best.

212
00:08:00,370 --> 00:08:02,620
I might be a little too old for it,

213
00:08:02,620 --> 00:08:05,410
but I stayed up ironing it all night.

214
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:07,500
Please, stop...

215
00:08:07,500 --> 00:08:08,420
Right,

216
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:09,370
(Sniff)
Right,

217
00:08:09,370 --> 00:08:11,870
(Sniff)
I'm already 30, after all.

218
00:08:11,870 --> 00:08:12,450
(Sniff)

219
00:08:12,450 --> 00:08:14,580
I know.

220
00:08:14,580 --> 00:08:16,680
You're 38!

221
00:08:16,680 --> 00:08:17,040
(Mix)
You're 38!

222
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:20,120
(Mix)
No, I just feel a little embarrassed.

223
00:08:20,120 --> 00:08:21,620
Anyway, shouldn't we get everything ready first?

224
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:22,660
Excuse me!

225
00:08:22,830 --> 00:08:23,870
Everyone's here!

226
00:08:24,250 --> 00:08:24,410
(Uh...)

227
00:08:24,410 --> 00:08:25,730
(Uh...)
Mom, hurry and go inside!

228
00:08:25,870 --> 00:08:28,250
- Mom?
- Come on in!

229
00:08:28,250 --> 00:08:29,950
Why did you come out?!

230
00:08:29,950 --> 00:08:31,830
How'd you bounce back so fast?!

231
00:08:31,830 --> 00:08:32,789
Well...

232
00:08:32,789 --> 00:08:35,000
But we can't keep your friends waiting!

233
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:36,159
Look down.

234
00:08:36,159 --> 00:08:37,409
Your outfit!

235
00:08:37,789 --> 00:08:39,120
I went to all this trouble to prepare it!

236
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:41,289
Let them see it just once!

237
00:08:41,289 --> 00:08:42,700
It'd be a shame otherwise!

238
00:08:42,700 --> 00:08:45,000
That one time could be your downfall!

239
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,160
- Do you even understand?!
- Sorry to intrude!

240
00:09:00,500 --> 00:09:03,540
N-No, that's not...

241
00:09:03,700 --> 00:09:07,040
(Entrance Ceremony)

242
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:08,940
(Entrance Ceremony)
Some Things Never Change.

243
00:09:08,940 --> 00:09:09,200
(Kotobuki Restaurant)

244
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:10,610
Anyway...

245
00:09:10,660 --> 00:09:13,000
(Komaro)
I'm Hisako's mom, Mayuki!

246
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,620
(Komaro)
It's nice to meet you all.

247
00:09:14,620 --> 00:09:15,790
Nice to meet you.

248
00:09:16,040 --> 00:09:18,620
I'm sorry for getting so carried away earlier.

249
00:09:18,620 --> 00:09:21,950
I got a little too worked up
when I heard everyone was coming.

250
00:09:21,950 --> 00:09:23,580
It's fine. I don't mind at all.

251
00:09:23,580 --> 00:09:25,000
I don't mind, either.

252
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:26,040
(The look on a high school girl's face
when her friend)

253
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:27,830
(spotted her mother's cosplay costumes and bra)
But the President...

254
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:29,580
Are you okay?

255
00:09:29,910 --> 00:09:31,750
Sorry. Thanks.

256
00:09:32,250 --> 00:09:34,250
Arisu.

257
00:09:34,250 --> 00:09:35,620
Yes?

258
00:09:35,620 --> 00:09:39,910
Are those two really a thing?

259
00:09:39,910 --> 00:09:42,640
(Excited!)
Well... How should I put it?

260
00:09:42,640 --> 00:09:42,950
Well... How should I put it?

261
00:09:42,950 --> 00:09:45,290
At that moment, Arisu thought...

262
00:09:45,290 --> 00:09:49,000
Maybe Ms. Mayuki had gotten the wrong idea.

263
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:52,200
She must've misunderstood something.

264
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:52,730
So, that's what happened, but...

265
00:09:52,730 --> 00:09:54,410
(Excited!)
So, that's what happened, but...

266
00:09:54,410 --> 00:09:54,940
(Excited!)
Yeah, probably.

267
00:09:54,940 --> 00:09:57,700
Yeah, probably.

268
00:09:58,200 --> 00:10:01,250
It sounded fun, so I decided to play along.

269
00:10:01,700 --> 00:10:03,200
Cooking begins.

270
00:10:03,410 --> 00:10:06,540
I've gathered a bunch of ingredients we could use.

271
00:10:06,540 --> 00:10:08,200
That's quite a lot!

272
