Is this salmon?

273
00:10:09,910 --> 00:10:10,750
Yep.

274
00:10:10,750 --> 00:10:13,200
I got the salmon scraps to keep the cost down!

275
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:14,200
I see.

276
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:15,370
As expected of the President!

277
00:10:15,370 --> 00:10:17,580
You're good at cooking, too.

278
00:10:17,910 --> 00:10:20,250
I'm still no match for you, Mizunoe.

279
00:10:20,250 --> 00:10:21,790
Arisu, look!

280
00:10:21,790 --> 00:10:25,330
Yeah, just like a married couple.

281
00:10:25,620 --> 00:10:27,040
Taste test.

282
00:10:27,540 --> 00:10:28,830
This broth is great!

283
00:10:28,830 --> 00:10:30,040
She's really got a knack for this!

284
00:10:30,040 --> 00:10:31,160
Absolutely.

285
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:32,500
As expected of the President.

286
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:33,910
This tastes amazing!

287
00:10:33,910 --> 00:10:35,250
This is delicious!

288
00:10:35,250 --> 00:10:36,250
My little girl...

289
00:10:36,250 --> 00:10:37,070
It's... good, isn't it?

290
00:10:37,070 --> 00:10:38,790
(Whispering)
It's... good, isn't it?

291
00:10:38,790 --> 00:10:39,750
(Whispering)
Yes!

292
00:10:39,750 --> 00:10:40,160
(Whispering)

293
00:10:40,160 --> 00:10:43,330
See? I told you!

294
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,000
Ume!

295
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:46,290
(Pulling)
Got it!

296
00:10:46,290 --> 00:10:46,370
Got it!

297
00:10:46,370 --> 00:10:48,000
Careful!

298
00:10:48,710 --> 00:10:48,870
(Startled!)

299
00:10:48,870 --> 00:10:49,790
(Startled!)
Arisu!

300
00:10:49,790 --> 00:10:51,000
(Startled!)
That girl is...

301
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:54,660
Yeah, just like a father and daughter.

302
00:10:55,370 --> 00:10:57,000
A father and daughter?

303
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:58,870
Yes. That's Komaro.

304
00:10:58,870 --> 00:11:00,830
Some people call them

305
00:11:00,830 --> 00:11:01,040
(Only Arisu)
Some people call them

306
00:11:01,040 --> 00:11:01,250
(Only Arisu)

307
00:11:01,250 --> 00:11:04,120
(Only Arisu)
Hisako Mommy, Ume Daddy, and little Komaro.

308
00:11:04,120 --> 00:11:04,330
(Only Arisu)

309
00:11:04,330 --> 00:11:05,250
So

310
00:11:05,250 --> 00:11:07,410
that makes her my granddaughter?

311
00:11:07,410 --> 00:11:09,350
That's right!

312
00:11:09,350 --> 00:11:09,830
(Hmm... Hmm...)
That's right!

313
00:11:09,830 --> 00:11:13,660
(Hmm... Hmm...)
Komaro, how about cooking with me?

314
00:11:13,660 --> 00:11:14,570
(Hmm... Hmm...)
Okay!

315
00:11:14,700 --> 00:11:18,280
(Shaping)

316
00:11:18,450 --> 00:11:19,620
Komaro!

317
00:11:19,620 --> 00:11:23,120
If you hold the rice like this, you
can shape it into a nice, neat rice ball.

318
00:11:23,120 --> 00:11:24,250
Like this?

319
00:11:24,250 --> 00:11:27,370
You want to shape it at a right angle like this.

320
00:11:27,620 --> 00:11:29,450
I see!

321
00:11:31,540 --> 00:11:33,420
So this is what having a granddaughter feels like!

322
00:11:33,420 --> 00:11:34,000
(1. Beef Tendon Stew
2. Salmon Trimmings)

323
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:35,660
(3. Chicken Breast Cutlet)
It's done!

324
00:11:36,040 --> 00:11:37,250
That looks great!

325
00:11:37,250 --> 00:11:38,580
It looks delicious!

326
00:11:38,580 --> 00:11:40,040
I'm glad!

327
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:41,540
All right, let's taste it!

328
00:11:41,540 --> 00:11:42,540
Okay!

329
00:11:43,450 --> 00:11:45,370
Let's eat!

330
00:11:45,370 --> 00:11:46,450
It's delicious!

331
00:11:46,450 --> 00:11:48,410
You did a perfect job!

332
00:11:48,750 --> 00:11:50,120
Yay!

333
00:11:50,660 --> 00:11:52,370
You've got rice stuck to your face.

334
00:11:52,370 --> 00:11:53,750
Thanks.

335
00:11:53,750 --> 00:11:55,750
Arisu, this...

336
00:11:55,750 --> 00:11:56,830
Yeah.

337
00:11:56,830 --> 00:11:58,660
That's a two-generation household.

338
00:11:58,660 --> 00:12:01,000
I knew it! What should I do?

339
00:12:01,370 --> 00:12:03,540
Thank you for all your help today.

340
00:12:03,540 --> 00:12:07,080
Thanks to you two, we've made a lot of progress.

341
00:12:07,080 --> 00:12:09,200
Not at all. We all made this happen.

342
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:11,750
Don't mention it.

343
00:12:12,200 --> 00:12:13,830
And, Ms. Mayuki...

344
00:12:15,160 --> 00:12:16,620
Next time, please...

345
00:12:16,830 --> 00:12:19,410
let me try your cooking, Ms. Mayuki.

346
00:12:19,410 --> 00:12:20,080
(He Means Restaurant)
let me try your cooking, Ms. Mayuki.

347
00:12:23,750 --> 00:12:24,660
Honey!

348
00:12:24,660 --> 00:12:27,580
Today, I got a granddaughter,

349
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:30,000
and I also got a confession!

350
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:30,750
Stop it!

351
00:12:30,750 --> 00:12:34,700
At 25, he married 18-year-old Mayuki,

352
00:12:34,700 --> 00:12:38,580
quit his job, and took over her family's business.

353
00:12:39,750 --> 00:12:40,750
All right!

354
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:41,870
(Affordable Rice Ball Proposal: )
It's done!

355
00:12:41,870 --> 00:12:43,500
(Affordable Rice Ball Proposal:)
The onigiri proposal is ready,

356
00:12:43,660 --> 00:12:45,370
thanks to the president and Ms. Mayuki!

357
00:12:45,370 --> 00:12:47,200
It all came together nicely!

358
00:12:47,200 --> 00:12:49,700
And they're even willing to handle the production.

359
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:51,870
We can't thank them enough!

360
00:12:52,040 --> 00:12:53,120
Leave it to me!

361
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:55,250
It's for Ume and my granddaughter, Komaro.

362
00:12:55,250 --> 00:12:56,910
And it'll be good publicity, too!

363
00:12:56,910 --> 00:12:58,080
Granddaughter?

364
00:12:58,080 --> 00:13:00,750
It'll be 70 yen each, including labor costs.

365
00:13:00,750 --> 00:13:03,870
That should make Michinoku's wish come true.

366
00:13:03,870 --> 00:13:05,700
That's a bargain by anyone's standards!

367
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:08,370
Now we just have to figure out how to sell them.

368
00:13:08,600 --> 00:13:09,040
(Administrative Office)

369
00:13:09,040 --> 00:13:10,060
(Administrative Office)
Ah, that's going to be a little difficult.

370
00:13:10,060 --> 00:13:10,080
Ah, that's going to be a little difficult.

371
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:13,160
(Administration Staff, Yoshino Saegusa)
Ah, that's going to be a little difficult.

372
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:13,790
Ah, that's going to be a little difficult.

373
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:16,250
W-Why?

374
00:13:16,250 --> 00:13:19,950
The school store is run by an outside contractor,

375
00:13:19,950 --> 00:13:23,540
so students aren't allowed to get involved.

376
00:13:23,540 --> 00:13:25,080
Isn't our school's philosophy

377
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:26,910
to value student initiative

378
00:13:26,910 --> 00:13:30,370
and support their efforts?

379
00:13:30,370 --> 00:13:32,790
I don't think this goes against that.

380
00:13:32,790 --> 00:13:35,700
We've already worked out a menu that's feasible.

381
00:13:35,700 --> 00:13:37,200
I understand. I really do.

382
00:13:37,200 --> 00:13:39,580
I appreciate how much effort you've put into this,

383
00:13:39,580 --> 00:13:41,410
but what if people stop buying
everything else because of the onigiri?

384
00:13:41,410 --> 00:13:42,790
That would be a problem, right?

385
00:13:42,790 --> 00:13:45,040
Business is tough everywhere right now,

386
00:13:45,040 --> 00:13:47,410
so the contractor would probably be in a bind, too.

387
00:13:47,410 --> 00:13:49,250
Well...

388
00:13:49,250 --> 00:13:50,660
By the way,

389
00:13:50,660 --> 00:13:52,700
the prices at our school store

390
00:13:52,700 --> 00:13:55,160
are considerably higher than average.

391
00:13:55,160 --> 00:13:57,580
How do you explain that?

392
00:13:58,330 --> 00:14:01,870
Yes, I suppose they are a little pricey.

393
00:14:02,040 --> 00:14:05,040
But prices depend on costs and location.

394
00:14:05,040 --> 00:14:06,870
That's up to the contractor.

395
00:14:06,870 --> 00:14:08,330
I don't know the details, either.

396
00:14:08,620 --> 00:14:11,000
Well, anyway, sorry!

397
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:11,910
Goodbye.

398
00:14:12,250 --> 00:14:15,330
Excuse me, about that file...

399
00:14:17,080 --> 00:14:18,580
This is a tough one.

400
00:14:18,580 --> 00:14:19,910
Yeah.

401
00:14:19,910 --> 00:14:22,500
Is there really nothing we can do?

402
00:14:22,500 --> 00:14:24,700
A win-win plan...

403
00:14:24,700 --> 00:14:26,120
No, a brilliant strategy!

404
00:14:26,120 --> 00:14:27,950
No, a game-changing plan!

405
00:14:28,160 --> 00:14:30,160
We have to figure something out
by the end of the school day.

406
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:31,100
(Squirm)

407
00:14:31,100 --> 00:14:31,370
(Plop!)

408
00:14:31,370 --> 00:14:32,620
(Plop!)
Michinoku!

409
00:14:32,620 --> 00:14:33,310
Yeah

410
00:14:33,310 --> 00:14:33,580
Yeah?

411
00:14:33,580 --> 00:14:34,910
When did you get here?

412
00:14:34,910 --> 00:14:36,540
Anyway, what's with that cloth?

413
00:14:36,540 --> 00:14:38,080
It's for the taste test.

414
00:14:38,830 --> 00:14:42,750
The Baseball Club said Onigiri was delicious.

415
00:14:42,950 --> 00:14:45,040
Oh... That's great, then.

416
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:45,790
Yeah!

417
00:14:45,790 --> 00:14:48,120
I made about 30 of them.

418
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:49,370
That's a lot!

419
00:14:49,370 --> 00:14:52,200
- Plain rice, and there's filling.
- They were gone in 30 seconds.

420
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:53,700
- We can't thank you enough.
- They must've been starving.

421
00:14:53,700 --> 00:14:55,080
By the way,

422
00:14:56,450 --> 00:14:58,830
Komaro, have you had lunch?

423
00:14:59,200 --> 00:15:00,620
I forgot.

424
00:15:00,620 --> 00:15:03,370
You made 30 Onigiri...

425
00:15:03,370 --> 00:15:05,620
Alright then, have some of my lunch.

426
00:15:05,620 --> 00:15:08,250
Ume, that problem you were having earlier...

427
00:15:08,250 --> 00:15:09,540
The onigiri?

428
00:15:10,410 --> 00:15:12,040
No... Well...

429
00:15:12,540 --> 00:15:13,700
...Yeah.

430
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:18,080
It's nothing.
We're still just in talks with Administration.

431
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:20,000
We've hit a bit of a snag.

432
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:23,080
But I'm going to do my best to convince them.

433
00:15:26,330 --> 00:15:27,870
I'm sorry.

434
00:15:31,950 --> 00:15:33,250
No.

435
00:15:33,250 --> 00:15:35,290
What are you apologizing for?

436
00:15:35,290 --> 00:15:38,080
It's only our first negotiation.

437
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:39,250
I may not look it,

438
00:15:39,250 --> 00:15:41,370
but I'm actually pretty good at negotiating.

439
00:15:41,580 --> 00:15:44,330
If we just talk things through,
I'm sure it'll work out.

440
00:15:44,330 --> 00:15:47,000
Right	. As long as we explain ourselves properly.

441
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:47,800
So I'm selling each one for 40 yen?

442
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:48,550
(Huh...)
So I'm selling each one for 40 yen?

443
00:15:48,550 --> 00:15:48,590
So I'm selling each one for 40 yen?

444
00:15:48,590 --> 00:15:49,010
(Ingredient Cost: 40 yen, Selling Price: 40 yen)
So I'm selling each one for 40 yen?

445
00:15:49,010 --> 00:15:49,370
So I'm selling each one for 40 yen?

446
00:15:49,370 --> 00:15:52,410
This is a request someone took the time
to put in the suggestion box.

447
00:15:56,950 --> 00:15:59,450
It's going to be fine. I promise!

448
00:16:03,290 --> 00:16:04,410
Ume...

449
00:16:05,330 --> 00:16:06,660
You're right.

450
00:16:06,830 --> 00:16:08,870
Exactly. We can do this.

451
00:16:08,950 --> 00:16:09,120
(Tan)

452
00:16:09,120 --> 00:16:10,870
(Tan)
Arisu? What's up?

453
00:16:10,870 --> 00:16:11,160
Arisu? What's up?

454
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:14,250
Shall we pull off an Ultra-C move?!

455
00:16:14,250 --> 00:16:14,820
(5-7-5-7-7)

456
00:16:18,830 --> 00:16:20,370
(General Affairs Office)

457
00:16:22,370 --> 00:16:23,500
Excuse us.

458
00:16:23,500 --> 00:16:23,540
Yes?

459
00:16:23,540 --> 00:16:23,920
(Creak)
Yes?

460
00:16:23,920 --> 00:16:24,540
Yes?

461
00:16:24,950 --> 00:16:28,000
You guys again?

462
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:31,120
Could you spare us a little more of your time?

463
00:16:31,660 --> 00:16:34,250
Do you all think
the Administration staff have nothing to do?

464
00:16:34,250 --> 00:16:35,870
I'm actually very busy.

465
00:16:37,580 --> 00:16:41,120
You've been embezzling money
from the school store vendors, haven't you?

466
00:16:41,120 --> 00:16:41,810
(Dear Ms. Saegusa:)

467
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:44,160
(Student Council Room)

468
00:16:44,160 --> 00:16:45,160
(Student Council Room)
Embezzling money?

469
00:16:45,160 --> 00:16:47,750
Yes. The bread sold at our school store

470
00:16:47,750 --> 00:16:50,160
has always been a little overpriced.

471
00:16:50,450 --> 00:16:52,120
And here's why.

472
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:53,500
Gift certificates?

473
00:16:53,500 --> 00:16:56,080
Apparently, that staff member brought them in

474
00:16:56,080 --> 00:17:00,410
and received gift certificates
in exchange for signing the contract.

475
00:17:00,410 --> 00:17:02,250
That's so tacky.

476
00:17:02,580 --> 00:17:05,829
If we confront her with this...

477
00:17:05,829 --> 00:17:07,790
(Mutter)

478
00:17:08,790 --> 00:17:10,119
Ugh, you're annoying.

479
00:17:10,500 --> 00:17:12,950
I thought you came charging in
with something important.

480
00:17:12,950 --> 00:17:16,200
Those were just coincidences! Coincidences!

481
00:17:16,200 --> 00:17:18,579
I simply forgot to report the gift certificates.

482
00:17:18,579 --> 00:17:20,950
There's absolutely nothing improper about it.

483
00:17:20,950 --> 00:17:22,950
You're making yourselves look ridiculous!

484
00:17:22,950 --> 00:17:23,430
Actually, you're pretty stupid.

485
00:17:23,430 --> 00:17:25,060
(Tap)
Actually, you're pretty stupid.

486
00:17:25,060 --> 00:17:25,750
Actually, you're pretty stupid.

487
00:17:25,750 --> 00:17:29,500
All the teachers love me, you know.

488
00:17:29,500 --> 00:17:31,000
You didn't even know that...?

489
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:32,410
Wait a minute...

490
00:17:32,410 --> 00:17:34,660
I don't know how you got your hands on this,

491
00:17:34,660 --> 00:17:35,490
(Slide)
Email hacking and attempted blackmail.

492
00:17:35,490 --> 00:17:36,950
Email hacking and attempted blackmail.

493
00:17:36,950 --> 00:17:40,290
I'll report it to the teachers.

494
00:17:40,290 --> 00:17:43,080
How underhanded! If this keeps up...

495
00:17:43,080 --> 00:17:45,000
I guess we have no choice.

496
00:17:45,910 --> 00:17:49,290
I really want to ○ Mr. Tanaka.

497
00:17:49,950 --> 00:17:51,330
Terui-senpai?

498
00:17:51,330 --> 00:17:54,290
The principal's bald head
is flawless. I worship it.

499
00:17:54,290 --> 00:17:56,660
A monkey came to watch,
so I squeezed my boobs together to make cleavage.

500
00:17:56,660 --> 00:17:57,660
That felt amazing!

501
00:17:57,660 --> 00:17:58,950
So excited, my little ○○!

502
00:17:58,950 --> 00:18:01,870
High school is a perfect little ○○ wonderland.

503
00:18:01,870 --> 00:18:04,200
She said most of those things late at night.

504
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:06,910
Maybe she got lonely after a few drinks?

505
00:18:06,910 --> 00:18:08,370
Then, could it be...?

506
00:18:09,950 --> 00:18:12,080
Where did you get those...?

507
00:18:12,080 --> 00:18:14,040
You have to be careful.

508
00:18:14,040 --> 00:18:17,040
Local brands are easy to trace.

509
00:18:17,040 --> 00:18:18,910
But still...

510
00:18:18,910 --> 00:18:21,540
Chicken... and so on...

511
00:18:21,540 --> 00:18:22,870
Oh, my...

512
00:18:23,160 --> 00:18:27,910
You're a beautiful woman, but you're so desperate.

513
00:18:29,450 --> 00:18:32,790
So, what do you think?
Are you going to go crying to the teachers?

514
00:18:33,080 --> 00:18:34,700
(Pant, Boing, Oh!)
N-No... there's no need for that...

515
00:18:34,700 --> 00:18:37,120
(Pant, Boing, Oh!)
Can we sell the Onigiri?

516
00:18:37,120 --> 00:18:38,620
I'll do everything I can.

517
00:18:38,620 --> 00:18:41,500
Will you do as we say from now on?

518
00:18:41,500 --> 00:18:42,790
Yes.

519
00:18:42,790 --> 00:18:43,620
Good grief.

520
00:18:43,620 --> 00:18:47,700
Mizunoe realized he should never cross this woman.

521
00:18:48,080 --> 00:18:49,620
Sorry for calling you over out of the blue.

522
00:18:49,620 --> 00:18:52,290
What is it? Why'd you call me?

523
00:18:52,540 --> 00:18:53,660
What's up?

524
00:18:53,660 --> 00:18:55,540
There's too much stuff.

525
00:18:56,160 --> 00:18:58,120
Be my step stool.

526
00:18:59,120 --> 00:19:00,160
(School Store)

527
00:19:00,450 --> 00:19:02,120
All right, finally...

528
00:19:02,290 --> 00:19:03,660
(Kotobuki Restaurant: )
The Onigiri Display Shelf!

529
00:19:03,660 --> 00:19:05,120
(Three Generations of Rice Balls)
It's done!

530
00:19:05,370 --> 00:19:07,870
Ms. Masaki's Three-Generation Onigiri.

531
00:19:07,870 --> 00:19:09,910
It's a little unconventional, but I like it!

532
00:19:10,080 --> 00:19:11,620
I made them!

533
00:19:11,620 --> 00:19:13,540
Three-Generation Onigiri.

534
00:19:13,540 --> 00:19:16,200
I was rooting for Komaro Onigiri, though.

535
00:19:17,160 --> 00:19:18,130
And thanks to Ms. Saegusa
for handling the register.

536
00:19:18,130 --> 00:19:21,080
(Cashier)
And thanks to Ms. Saegusa
for handling the register.

537
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:22,580
(Cashier)
You're such a pain.

538
00:19:22,580 --> 00:19:23,950
At least show me some respect.

539
00:19:23,950 --> 00:19:25,910
(Three Generations)
Honestly, why do I have to...

540
00:19:25,910 --> 00:19:28,080
Sorry, we're short-staffed.

541
00:19:28,080 --> 00:19:31,160
Isn't there someone more qualified for this?

542
00:19:31,160 --> 00:19:34,200
I did graduate from a national university, you know.

543
00:19:34,200 --> 00:19:35,290
That's true.

544
00:19:35,290 --> 00:19:37,790
But Ms. Saegusa might embezzle the money.

545
00:19:37,790 --> 00:19:39,910
I wouldn't! Don't say that out loud!

546
00:19:40,160 --> 00:19:42,950
Damn it, are these 10-yen coins
enough to make change?

547
00:19:42,950 --> 00:19:44,040
(Japanese Rice Balls)
All right.

548
00:19:44,040 --> 00:19:46,200
(Japanese Rice Balls)
Think she'll do a good job?

549
00:19:46,370 --> 00:19:46,450
(Thump, Thump, Thump, Thump)

550
00:19:46,450 --> 00:19:48,160
(Thump, Thump, Thump, Thump)
- Open. - All right!

551
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:50,660
(Thump, Thump, Thump, Thump)
You're finally open! Let's show our support!

552
00:19:50,660 --> 00:19:52,660
- Everyone from the Swimming Club!
- The Student Council's always helped us out.

553
00:19:52,660 --> 00:19:54,160
They're cheap, and they look delicious!

554
00:19:54,160 --> 00:19:56,160
All right, everyone! Buy as many as you can!

555
00:19:56,160 --> 00:19:57,660
Thanks for your purchase!

556
00:19:57,660 --> 00:19:59,380
(Clink)

557
00:20:00,450 --> 00:20:01,700
Want me to cover it for now?

558
00:20:01,700 --> 00:20:03,080
- Hey!
- Woohoo!

559
00:20:03,080 --> 00:20:04,250
Hello!

560
00:20:04,250 --> 00:20:05,580
What's going on here?

561
00:20:05,580 --> 00:20:08,370
It's the Student Council's onigiri sale!

562
00:20:09,660 --> 00:20:11,330
Then I'll take two.

563
00:20:11,580 --> 00:20:13,160
Anyway, good luck!

564
00:20:13,160 --> 00:20:14,870
Thank you! Come again!

565
00:20:15,160 --> 00:20:17,290
She already bought some bread, though.

566
00:20:17,290 --> 00:20:18,290
It's delicious!

567
00:20:18,290 --> 00:20:21,290
She's just showing her support.
She's just acting all cool.

568
00:20:21,290 --> 00:20:22,950
Come on, don't be so cynical.

569
00:20:23,200 --> 00:20:25,080
More and more people are gathering!

570
00:20:25,080 --> 00:20:27,120
It's really picking up, Michinoku!

571
00:20:27,330 --> 00:20:28,870
Hey, Ume!

572
00:20:28,870 --> 00:20:30,910
Can I get three?

573
00:20:30,910 --> 00:20:31,950
Batsunosuke.

574
00:20:31,950 --> 00:20:33,000
You want three?

575
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:34,790
Thanks for buying so many!

576
00:20:35,620 --> 00:20:37,660
I'm picking these up for the Robotics Club.

577
00:20:37,660 --> 00:20:39,080
I really...

578
00:20:39,370 --> 00:20:41,120
feel bad about this.

579
00:20:41,120 --> 00:20:44,750
I guess buying them for people
who aren't even here is kind of unfair.

580
00:20:44,750 --> 00:20:47,950
And buying three at once is pretty greedy, too.

581
00:20:47,950 --> 00:20:49,660
Thanks! That'll be 210 yen.

582
00:20:50,500 --> 00:20:51,580
Three-Generation Onigiri...

583
00:20:51,580 --> 00:20:52,370
Baseball Club.

584
00:20:52,370 --> 00:20:53,200
Five, please!

585
00:20:53,200 --> 00:20:54,290
Six!

586
00:20:54,290 --> 00:20:55,230
Coming right up!

587
00:20:55,230 --> 00:20:55,580
(Chomp!)
Coming right up!

588
00:20:55,580 --> 00:20:55,830
(Chomp!)

589
00:20:55,830 --> 00:20:57,370
- They're a huge hit!
- They're delicious!

590
00:20:57,370 --> 00:20:59,080
The rice... It's so good...

591
00:20:59,080 --> 00:21:00,660
I'm finally full...

592
00:21:00,660 --> 00:21:02,200
Were they starving or something?

593
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:02,700
(Munch)

594
00:21:02,700 --> 00:21:04,250
These are really good!

595
00:21:04,250 --> 00:21:05,200
Miss!

596
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:07,330
I can't believe they're this cheap!

597
00:21:07,330 --> 00:21:09,160
No wonder they're selling like crazy.

598
00:21:09,160 --> 00:21:11,950
You even got the stubborn
administration staff on board.

599
00:21:11,950 --> 00:21:13,580
(Tingle!)
You all really worked hard.

600
00:21:13,580 --> 00:21:13,870
You all really worked hard.

601
00:21:13,870 --> 00:21:16,660
- Miss, have you paid for yours yet?
- I helped out too, you know, Michinoku.

602
00:21:19,500 --> 00:21:21,620
Wow, they're almost sold out!

603
00:21:21,620 --> 00:21:22,950
Yeah.

604
00:21:22,950 --> 00:21:25,160
But I'm exhausted.

605
00:21:25,160 --> 00:21:26,540
Yeah...

606
00:21:26,540 --> 00:21:28,450
Michinoku, you can take a break now...

607
00:21:28,450 --> 00:21:30,120
Onigiri?

608
00:21:30,540 --> 00:21:32,660
Those look good. I'll take one.

609
00:21:32,660 --> 00:21:33,700
Sure!

610
00:21:33,910 --> 00:21:36,700
We're still selling! Come take a look!

611
00:21:36,700 --> 00:21:37,910
Okay!

612
00:21:43,450 --> 00:21:45,830
I'm glad we managed to make this project happen.

613
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:47,160
Yeah.

614
00:21:47,450 --> 00:21:49,000
(Hmm...)
Hey, about that bread...

615
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:50,830
(Hmm...)
No thanks. Eat it yourself.

616
00:21:50,830 --> 00:21:53,040
That's what you get for showing off.

617
00:21:53,040 --> 00:21:54,580
I'm stuffed.

618
00:21:54,580 --> 00:21:56,450
(Hahaha!)
You still have another mouth down there.

619
00:21:56,450 --> 00:21:58,120
(Hahaha!)
You're so vulgar...

620
00:21:58,120 --> 00:21:59,080
(Hahaha!)

621
00:21:59,120 --> 00:21:59,290
(Enjoyed them immensely after this)

622
00:21:59,290 --> 00:22:00,910
(Enjoyed them immensely after this)
Want to eat with your other mouth?

623
00:22:00,910 --> 00:22:03,120
(Enjoyed them immensely after this)
Honestly... Fine, I'll help you.

624
00:22:03,120 --> 00:22:04,910
I think I'll just take it home.

625
